+# ArcheOne (XOne) - Android Project Context
+
+## Project Overview
+**ArcheOne** (internal project name: **XOne**) is a Kotlin-based Android application designed for enterprise and employee management. It features a modern UI built with **Jetpack Compose** and includes modules for employee engagement, facility management, and productivity tools.
+
+### Key Features
+*   **Employee Services:** Business Cards, Holiday Calendar, Policies, Greetings, and Global Celebrations.
+*   **Facility Management:** "Meet Space" (Meeting Room booking), "Desk Cart" (Stationary ordering), Inventory, and Asset Management.
+*   **Safety & Support:** SOS (Emergency), Chat Support, Raise a Concern, and Track Tickets.
+*   **Security:** Biometric Authentication, MPIN setup, and secure document viewing.
+
+## Tech Stack
+*   **Language:** Kotlin (JVM Target 11)
+*   **UI Framework:** Jetpack Compose (Material 3 & Material 2)
+*   **Architecture Pattern:** MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel) - *Inferred standard for Compose*
+*   **Build System:** Gradle (Kotlin DSL)
+*   **Networking:** Retrofit, OkHttp, Gson
+*   **Image Loading:** Coil
+*   **Local Storage:** Room Database
+*   **Other Libraries:** CameraX, MLKit (Barcode Scanning), WebKit, Lottie Animations, Google Generative AI.
+
+## Project Structure
+*   **Root:** `.`
+*   **App Module:** `app/`
+    *   **Source:** `app/src/main/java/com/archeGlobal/one/`
+        *   Contains Activities, Screens, and logic for all features.
+    *   **Resources:** `app/src/main/res/`
+        *   Layouts (limited usage due to Compose), Drawables, Values, and XML configurations.
+    *   **Manifest:** `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`
+        *   Defines `SplashActivity` as the entry point (via `SplashAlias`).
+        *   Lists all application activities and required permissions (Camera, Storage, Internet).
+
+## Building and Running
+
+### Prerequisites
+*   **JDK 11+** (Project targets JVM 11, compileSDK 36).
+*   **Environment Note:** The local environment requires a specific `JAVA_HOME` configuration for Gradle to function correctly.
+
+### Key Commands
+**Note:** Always prepend the `JAVA_HOME` configuration to Gradle commands in this environment.
+
+*   **Build Debug APK:**
+    ```powershell
+    $env:JAVA_HOME="C:\Program Files\JetBrains\IntelliJ IDEA 2025.3.1.1\jbr"; ./gradlew assembleDebug
+    ```
+
+*   **Install to Device:**
+    ```powershell
+    $env:JAVA_HOME="C:\Program Files\JetBrains\IntelliJ IDEA 2025.3.1.1\jbr"; ./gradlew installDebug
+    ```
+
+*   **Clean Build:**
+    ```powershell
+    $env:JAVA_HOME="C:\Program Files\JetBrains\IntelliJ IDEA 2025.3.1.1\jbr"; ./gradlew clean
+    ```
+
+## Development Conventions
+*   **Code Style:** Follows standard Kotlin conventions. `ktlint` is integrated for linting.
+*   **Configuration:**
+    *   `build.gradle.kts`: Dependencies and SDK versions.
+    *   `gradle.properties`: Used for sensitive signing credentials (RELEASE_STORE_FILE, RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD, etc.).
+*   **Namespace:** `com.archeGlobal.one`
+
+## Recent Context (from Memories)
+*   **Biometrics:** The app supports "Device Security" (Biometric OR Device Credential) for app locking.
+*   **Edge-to-Edge:** `MainActivity` is configured for edge-to-edge display.
+*   **Helper Classes:** Centralized `ImageUtils` and `createCategoriesMap` are used to reduce code duplication.
